Description: adaptive caching DNS forwarder for single-egress networks
 EgressDNS is a caching DNS forwarder for enterprise LANs that reach the Internet
 through a single egress. It forwards over UDP, TCP, DNS-over-TLS, DNS-over-HTTPS
 (HTTP/2 and HTTP/3) and DNS-over-QUIC, validates DNSSEC, and adapts its upstream
 selection and answer ordering to measurements taken on the live network.
 .
 All measurement is background work: a client query is never blocked on a probe, a
 dataset refresh or a prediction. If every adaptive subsystem fails, the daemon
 degrades to a correct caching forwarder rather than failing.
 .
 It performs no answer synthesis of any kind - no DNS64, no synthetic CNAMEs, no
 AAAA suppression - and never returns third-party proxy or relay addresses.
